cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the CatCrypt paper below."
title: "CatCrypt: From Rust to Cryptographic Security in Lean"
abstract: >-
  A compiler for cryptographic code written in Lean 4 with its correctness
  proofs. Its compile line takes a hax-extracted Rust module through typed
  dialects over the Com IR to x86-64 machine bytes, which the package's own
  decoder reads and its own x86-64 model runs. Value correctness is proved for
  every result, and constant time for every result under hypotheses on the
  translated source. Instruction selection to AArch64 and RV64
  is proved for straight-line code over virtual registers, without register
  allocation.
type: software
authors:
